# The Dockerfile only copies shiny-server/, but everything here is still sent to
# the daemon as build context, so keep it small.

.git
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/._*

# The deployer's own configuration. It is bind-mounted at /app/config.R at
# runtime, so baking a copy in only risks shipping somebody's local paths, and
# means an image run without the mount silently uses a developer's settings
# instead of saying the config is missing. R/09_config.R already explains what
# to do when it is absent.
shiny-server/config.R

# Data, not code. The example dataset is for running CRAVE, not for building it.
example-dataset/
example-analysis/
images/
*.tar.gz

# Runtime state a dataset accumulates: the metadata cache, and everything the
# Submit tab keeps (workbooks, counts matrices, result tables, job logs). Neither
# belongs in an image, and the submission area can be large.
**/.crave-cache/
**/.crave-submit/

# Development leftovers
tools/
**/.Rhistory
**/.RData
**/.Rproj.user/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Documentation is not needed at runtime
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
docker-compose.yml
build-and-push.sh
